WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.530
Yesterday, the Council held its monthly meeting
for July.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.070
First on the agenda, was the renovation of
the Oxford Museum and Jaycee Building.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.810
The Council approved a new entrance and toilets
for the building with a budget of $125,000,

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:24.450
with $15,000 being contributed by the Oxford
Museum.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:28.880
The new entranceway will access the Museum
from the carpark on the western wall of the building.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.420
The Council also approved the Draft Kaiapoi
Town Centre Plan for public consultation.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:40.820
This document, will for the first time, plan
for the future of the Mixed-Use Business Areas,

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.969
formerly residential redzone and find ways
to integrate them into the current Town Centre.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:50.489
The consultation will be widely advertised
in Kaiapoi and nearby townships and is expected

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:51.980
to take place over August.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.640
The multi-use indoor sports facility took
another step forward yesterday as Councillors

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.150
approved staff to engage architects Warren
and Mahoney and quantity surveying firm, AECOM.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.350
After the design phase is underway, the Council
will put the procurement and construction

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.820
stages out to tender, with completion of the
facility targeted for the end of 2020.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:18.940
Councillors also approved contracting out
the operations and maintenance of Southbrook

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:23.800
Resource Recovery Park and Oxford Transfer
station to a private waste business, with

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.910
the option of having a community group manage
the resource recovery activities.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.960
This is similar to the existing contracts,
however it will also allow the council and

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.060
contractor to partner with a community organisation
to reduce waste.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:42.180
The Council was also updated on the rollout of the expanded Your Choice Kerbside Collection service.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.380
In the coming weeks, owners of properties
in kerbside collection areas will be receiving

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.840
a card which will allow them to select which collection service they would like for their property.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.040
The service is expected to start operation
from July next year.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.040
The next Council meeting will take place on
Tuesday 7th of August.

